<http://data.silknow.org/object/ac4ba176-2ef9-348b-95d7-6f28197b4b87>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Doublet for an older boy or young man, c.1625, English; Black silk grosgrain, trimmed with black silk bobbin lace"@en , "Doublet for an older boy or young man, of black silk grosgrain, interlined with linen and lined with black silk twill.  It has a 2¼-inch (5.4 cm) collar, ½-inch (1.25 cm) deep shoulder wings, curving 2-piece sleeves, with a high waist and 8 laps below the waist.  The belly pieces are made of pasteboard stitched between layers of linen and covered with the black silk twill.  The doublet is decorated with ⅜-inch (8 mm) wide black silk bobbin lace, in parallel rows of 3, edging the seams and laps, under the armholes, on the fronts.  A single row of lace covers the shoulder wings.  There are 4 worked buttonholes on each sleeve, 24 on the left front and 4 button loops of braided black silk on the left collar.  The buttons have a domed wooden core covered with black silk floss; only the core of 2 remain.  Inside at the waist is a band of linen covered with black silk twill, with 12 metal eyes. There is a separate tab of black silk with a single metal eye at the inside waist of each front.\n\nThe black silk is disintegrating and there are large areas where it is completely lost."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/12fb0f9f-20f2-3e9b-a315-a5866fa195bd> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Doublet for an older boy or young man, of black silk grosgrain, interlined with linen and lined with black silk twill.  It has a 2¼-inch (5.4 cm) collar, ½-inch (1.25 cm) deep shoulder wings, curving 2-piece sleeves, with a high waist and 8 laps below the waist.  The belly pieces are made of pasteboard stitched between layers of linen and covered with the black silk twill.  The doublet is decorated with ⅜-inch (8 mm) wide black silk bobbin lace, in parallel rows of 3, edging the seams and laps, under the armholes, on the fronts.  A single row of lace covers the shoulder wings.  There are 4 worked buttonholes on each sleeve, 24 on the left front and 4 button loops of braided black silk on the left collar.  The buttons have a domed wooden core covered with black silk floss; only the core of 2 remain.  Inside at the waist is a band of linen covered with black silk twill, with 12 metal eyes. There is a separate tab of black silk with a single metal eye at the inside waist of each front.\n\nThe black silk is disintegrating and there are large areas where it is completely lost."@en , "Doublet for an older boy or young man, c.1625, English; Black silk grosgrain, trimmed with black silk bobbin lace"@en ;
